    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0145",
      "reading_order": 190,
      "section": "Description",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 92.54999999999998,
        "t": 177.4801,
        "r": 533.6093000000009,
        "b": 138.9031
      },
      "content": "In air receiver/oil separator (AR), most of the oil is removed from the air/oil mixture by centrifugal action.The rest is removed by oil separator (OS). The oil collects in the lower part of air receiver/oil separator (AR),which serves as an oil tank.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_189",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_2",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_2",
          "title": "2       General description"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_189",
          "title": "Description"
        }
      ],
      "page": 19,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0146",
      "reading_order": 191,
      "section": "Description",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 92.54999999999998,
        "t": 131.94010000000003,
        "r": 552.3455999999992,
        "b": 106.56310000000008
      },
      "content": "The oil system is provided with a thermostatic bypass valve (BV). When the oil temperature is below its set point, bypass valve (BV) shuts off the supply to oil cooler (Co) and the oil cooler is bypassed.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_189",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_2",
      "section_level": 2,
